Avoid Emscripten's slow client-index upload path for polygon-mode lines.

gl4es emulates glPolygonMode(GL_LINE) by constructing a temporary edge index
array and issuing glDrawElements. With Emscripten FULL_ES2 and client-side
vertex arrays, every such draw uploads the indices and scans them in
JavaScript to discover the vertex range it must also upload. Immediate-mode
renderlists make that happen for every list, every frame; many small line
draws spend tens of milliseconds in ELEMENT_ARRAY_BUFFER bufferSubData calls.

For the GLES2+ path, preserve gl4es's existing edge generation but expand all
enabled client attributes in edge-index order and issue glDrawArrays(GL_LINES).
This trades modest extra vertex bytes and CPU copies for Emscripten's much
cheaper client-array upload path. GLES1 keeps the indexed path because it may
synthesize final colors and texture coordinates later in draw_renderlist.

The expansion retains vertices, normals, primary/secondary colors, fog
coordinates, and every texture-coordinate set. Allocation failure falls back
to the original indexed draw. Persistent display-list VBO state is not
mutated by the temporary client arrays.

Applied by scripts/web-deps.sh after cloning the pinned gl4es checkout.
